{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Module: Projects  (installed work — the proof photographs)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:            Show what OTODOR has actually fitted, in real doors, at
                      real addresses. Testimonials are what people say; this
                      is what the work looks like.
  Primary source:     A Shopify BLOG, one article per project — because this
                      content has to appear in two places at once (the
                      Projects page and the homepage) and blocks live in a
                      template, so a block-built gallery would have to be
                      uploaded twice and would drift apart the first time one
                      copy was edited. A blog is authored once and read by
                      every placement.
                        article.title           → project name
                        article.image           → cover photo
                        article.excerpt/content → the supporting line
                        article.tags.first      → the meta line (or the
                                                  metafield below)
                        custom.project_location → the meta line   [optional]
                        custom.project_video    → a video         [optional]
  Fallback order:     blog → `project` blocks → hide. `source` forces either.
  Visibility rule:    Renders only when at least one entry has a title. An
                      empty gallery is worse than no gallery, so the section
                      and its heading disappear together.
  Merchant editable:  YES — source, blog, headings, count, columns, colour
                      scheme, the "view all" action, every block field.
  Required metafields: none.
  Optional metafields: article `custom.project_location` (single line text),
                       `custom.project_video` (file_reference → a video).
                       Both optional: without them a project still renders
                       from the article's own title, image and tags.
  Dependencies:       snippets/otodor-project-card (the one card
                      implementation), snippets/otodor-icon, base.css tokens.
  Placement:          templates/page.projects.json (the full gallery) and
                      index.json (a short cut of the same blog + View all).
  Accessibility:      Each card is one article with a real heading; a linked
                      card uses a stretched overlay link with an accessible
                      name, so the whole tile is clickable without nesting
                      interactive elements inside a link. The mobile rail is
                      a labelled, keyboard-scrollable region.
  Reusable for:       Homepage, Projects page, a collection landing
                      ("wooden doors we have fitted"), an About page.

  ONE SECTION, TWO CONFIGURATIONS — exactly like otodor-banner. The homepage
  instance sets a limit and a View-all link; the Projects page shows the lot.
  Neither holds the content, so neither can go stale.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign scheme = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'light'
  assign limit = section.settings.limit | default: 9
  assign source = section.settings.source | default: 'auto'
  assign cols = section.settings.columns_desktop | default: 3

  # ── 1. READ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # `where` on a block list, then a blog, so `auto` prefers the shared
  # source and falls back to whatever this template carries itself.
  assign project_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'project'
  assign articles = nil
  if source != 'blocks' and section.settings.blog != blank
    assign articles = section.settings.blog.articles
  endif

  assign use_blog = false
  if articles != blank and articles.size > 0 and source != 'blocks'
    assign use_blog = true
  endif

  # ── 2. VALIDATE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # A block only counts once it has a title; an article always has one.
  assign usable = 0
  if use_blog
    assign usable = articles.size
  else
    for block in project_blocks
      if block.settings.title != blank
        assign usable = usable | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if usable > 0 -%}

{%- style -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} {
    padding-block: var(--otodor-section-py);
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--light {
    background: var(--otodor-bg-light); color: var(--otodor-ink);
    --pj-accent: var(--otodor-accent-on-light);
    --pj-soft: var(--otodor-ink-soft);
    --pj-rule: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    --pj-frame: var(--otodor-plinth);
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--dark {
    background: var(--otodor-black); color: var(--otodor-white);
    --pj-accent: var(--otodor-blue);
    --pj-soft: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.58);
    --pj-rule: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    --pj-frame: var(--otodor-surface);
  }

  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__inner {
    max-width: var(--otodor-container);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--otodor-header-mb);
    max-width: 60rem;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__eyebrow {
    display: block; font-family: var(--otodor-font-display);
    font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-widest); color: var(--pj-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--otodor-header-gap);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Declared, not inherited: Dawn sets colour directly on h1–h6, and a
    declared value always beats an inherited one — the bug that put a white
    heading on a light band in STEP 12.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__heading {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-4xl);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: var(--otodor-leading-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-tight); margin: 0;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--light .otodor-projects__heading { color: var(--otodor-ink); }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--dark .otodor-projects__heading { color: var(--otodor-white); }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__heading .accent { color: var(--pj-accent); }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__sub {
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-md); line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--pj-soft); max-width: 46rem;
  }

  /* ─ Grid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Desktop is a real grid inside the container so the cards' outer edges
     line up with every other section. Below 900px the same cards become a
     swipe rail — a project photograph needs width, and two 160px thumbs of
     a door tell you nothing. Same treatment as the testimonials. */
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat({{ cols }}, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1099px) {
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__rail {
      overflow-x: auto;
      scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
      scrollbar-width: none;
      margin-inline: -1.5rem;
      padding-inline: 1.5rem;
      /* Without this the snapport is the padding box and the first card
         snaps a gutter to the left of every other section. */
      scroll-padding-inline: 1.5rem;
    }
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__rail::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__grid {
      display: flex; width: max-content;
    }
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project {
      scroll-snap-align: start; width: min(80vw, 34rem);
    }
  }

  /* ─ Card ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     No card chrome: the photograph is the card. A border and a raised panel
     around a photo is two frames around one image. */
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project {
    position: relative; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem; min-width: 0;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__frame {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-md);
    background: var(--pj-frame);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__media {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block;
    transition: transform var(--otodor-dur-slow) var(--otodor-ease-out);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    The lift is on the image inside a fixed frame, so neighbouring cards
    never move and the grid row cannot reflow on hover.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project:hover .otodor-project__media { transform: scale(1.03); }
  {%- comment -%} A <video> must not be scaled — the controls would be cropped by the frame. {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project--video:hover .otodor-project__media { transform: none; }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__badge {
    position: absolute; top: 0.9rem; left: 0.9rem;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem; border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-pill);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.62); color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs);
    font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-wide); text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    The stretched link: the whole tile is clickable, but the link element
    itself stays outside the heading and the media, so nothing interactive
    is nested inside it — a <video>'s controls in particular stay usable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `display: block` is load-bearing, not tidiness. Dawn's base.css carries
    `a:empty { display: none }`, and a stretched overlay link is by definition
    an empty <a> — without this the whole card is unclickable and every click
    lands on the image behind it. Measured: 0 × 0 box, hit-test returning the
    <img>. Any future overlay link in this theme needs the same line.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__link {
    display: block;
    position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 2; border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-md);
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__link:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--pj-accent); outline-offset: 3px;
  }
  {%- comment -%} Video cards link from the title instead — see the card snippet. {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__title-link {
    color: inherit; text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out);
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__title-link:hover { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__body { display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__meta {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs);
    font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-wider); color: var(--pj-accent);
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__title {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-lg);
    font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-base); margin: 0;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--light .otodor-project__title { color: var(--otodor-ink); }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}.otodor-projects--dark .otodor-project__title { color: var(--otodor-white); }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__text {
    margin: 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--pj-soft);
    display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 3; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─ View all ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__footer {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--pj-rule);
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;
  }
  #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-projects__footer-note {
    margin: 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm); color: var(--pj-soft); flex: 1 1 16rem;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project__media { transition: none; }
    #otodor-projects-{{ section.id }} .otodor-project:hover .otodor-project__media { transform: none; }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section
  id="otodor-projects-{{ section.id }}"
  class="otodor-projects otodor-projects--{{ scheme }}"
  data-otodor-section="projects"
  aria-labelledby="otodor-projects-title-{{ section.id }}"
>
  <div class="otodor-projects__inner">
    <div class="otodor-projects__header" data-otodor-reveal="fade-up">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <span class="otodor-projects__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="otodor-projects__heading" id="otodor-projects-title-{{ section.id }}">
        {{ section.settings.heading | escape }}{% if section.settings.heading_accent != blank %} <span class="accent">{{ section.settings.heading_accent | escape }}</span>{% endif %}
      </h2>
      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="otodor-projects__sub">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div
      class="otodor-projects__rail"
      role="region"
      aria-labelledby="otodor-projects-title-{{ section.id }}"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <div class="otodor-projects__grid" data-otodor-reveal="fade-up">
        {%- if use_blog -%}
          {%- for article in articles limit: limit -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign pj_meta = article.metafields.custom.project_location
              if pj_meta == blank
                assign pj_meta = article.tags.first
              endif
              assign pj_video = article.metafields.custom.project_video.value
            -%}
            {%- render 'otodor-project-card',
              title: article.title,
              meta: pj_meta,
              text: article.excerpt_or_content,
              image: article.image,
              video: pj_video,
              link: article.url,
              sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 80vw' -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for block in project_blocks limit: limit -%}
            {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
              {%- render 'otodor-project-card',
                title: block.settings.title,
                meta: block.settings.meta,
                text: block.settings.text,
                image: block.settings.image,
                video: block.settings.video,
                video_url: block.settings.video_url,
                link: block.settings.link,
                sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 80vw' -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.view_all_label != blank -%}
      <div class="otodor-projects__footer">
        {%- if section.settings.footer_note != blank -%}
          <p class="otodor-projects__footer-note">{{ section.settings.footer_note | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a class="otodor-btn otodor-btn--{% if scheme == 'dark' %}ghost{% else %}outline{% endif %}"
           href="{{ section.settings.view_all_link | default: '/pages/projects' }}">
          {{ section.settings.view_all_label | escape }}
          <span class="otodor-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "OTODOR Projects",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Installed work — photographs and films of real OTODOR jobs. Author each project once as an article in a blog and every placement (this page, the homepage) reads the same source. Blocks below are the fallback for a one-off gallery." },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "source", "label": "Where projects come from", "default": "auto",
      "options": [
        { "value": "auto", "label": "Automatic — blog, then blocks" },
        { "value": "blog", "label": "Blog only" },
        { "value": "blocks", "label": "Blocks only" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "blog", "id": "blog", "label": "Projects blog", "info": "Create a blog (e.g. \"Projects\") and add one article per project. Article image = cover; first tag = the line above the name; optional article metafields custom.project_location and custom.project_video." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "limit", "label": "Maximum projects shown", "min": 3, "max": 24, "step": 1, "default": 9 },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "columns_desktop", "label": "Columns (desktop)", "default": "3",
      "options": [
        { "value": "2", "label": "2" },
        { "value": "3", "label": "3" },
        { "value": "4", "label": "4" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour scheme", "default": "light",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Light (off-white)" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Dark" }
      ]
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our Projects" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Doors we have" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading_accent", "label": "Heading accent (coloured)", "default": "already secured." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading", "default": "Homes, offices and apartment towers across India — surveyed, fitted and supported by OTODOR technicians." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "View all" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "footer_note", "label": "Note beside the button" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "view_all_label", "label": "Button label", "info": "Leave blank to hide the button — do that on the Projects page itself." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "view_all_link", "label": "Button link", "info": "Defaults to /pages/projects." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "project",
      "name": "Project",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Media cascade: Video wins, then Video link, then Image. The image is also the poster frame for either video." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Project name", "info": "Required — a block without one is skipped." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "meta", "label": "Line above the name", "info": "Location, door type, year — e.g. \"Bandra West, Mumbai\"." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Supporting line" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "1. Image" },
        { "type": "video", "id": "video", "label": "2. Video", "info": "Upload in Content → Files. Plays inline, served by Shopify's CDN." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "video_url", "label": "3. Video link", "info": "A direct .mp4 / .webm / .mov URL. Not a YouTube or Instagram page link." },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link", "info": "Optional. Makes the whole card clickable." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "OTODOR Projects",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "project" },
        { "type": "project" },
        { "type": "project" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
